1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,667
Total bubble. Prices have to come down.

2
00:00:03,667 --> 00:00:05,967
Stamp right here, please.

3
00:00:05,967 --> 00:00:07,900
There. Now it only goes up!

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:12,867
Before buying: a bubble. After buying: rock bottom. Double standard, number one.

5
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:15,433
I'm… Modapman.

6
00:00:17,433 --> 00:00:22,067
Case summary. Saturday morning, the neighborhood realtor. Two months before our jeonse lease ends.

7
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:24,300
You said we were just looking. Why did you stamp it?

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,233
So, how much is our place worth now?

9
00:00:26,233 --> 00:00:27,467
You bought it one minute ago.

10
00:00:27,467 --> 00:00:30,267
Just three rounds. Round one: asking prices.

11
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:31,567
Dad, what's an asking price?

12
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:35,133
Just what the seller wishes for. It's only real once it sells.

13
00:00:35,133 --> 00:00:36,967
Whoa, the next building just listed at this price!

14
00:00:36,967 --> 00:00:39,500
So that's our price now too. So what~

15
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,967
Their asking price: wishful thinking. Ours: the market price. Double standard, number two.

16
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:47,400
When what's yours looks pricier. It's called the endowment effect.

17
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,800
Endow… what?

18
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,400
The complex group chat says nobody list below this. Like!

19
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,267
That's price-fixing. It's against the law.

20
00:00:56,267 --> 00:00:58,200
Round two: "good news" and banners.

21
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:02,100
A new station in some other town? That takes ten years. All hype.

22
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,300
Dad, they say a station's coming to OUR town!

23
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:08,767
It's official! A station, a mall, our house turns to gold!

24
00:01:08,767 --> 00:01:10,733
A banner is not a confirmation.

25
00:01:10,733 --> 00:01:14,667
Believing only the news you want. Confirmation bias. Double standard, number three.

26
00:01:14,667 --> 00:01:19,100
An incinerator next town over? We need those. Opposing it is selfish.

27
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:20,867
Honey, it's in our town.

28
00:01:20,867 --> 00:01:23,300
Over my dead body! Not in our town!

29
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:27,067
Anywhere but my backyard: NIMBY. Double standard, number four.

30
00:01:27,067 --> 00:01:30,700
If every town says "not here"… where do we build it?

31
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,300
Round three: borrowing to the max, and interest.

32
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,467
Dude, I bought a place too. Borrowed every last won.

33
00:01:35,467 --> 00:01:39,400
Every last won? That's reckless. Can you handle the interest?

34
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,267
We maxed out our loan too.

35
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:44,400
Ours is leverage. Strategy. So what~

36
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,333
Dad, you said rent is money thrown away.

37
00:01:47,333 --> 00:01:50,300
Interest is different! It's… an investment cost!

38
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:56,333
When they do it, it's reckless. When I do it, it's leverage. Double standard, five and six.

39
00:01:56,333 --> 00:02:00,167
"I'll be the one who's fine." That's called optimism bias.

40
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:00,767
…Huh?

41
00:02:01,567 --> 00:02:04,100
Bonus round. Rapid-fire double standards!

42
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:07,233
Their complex: too crowded. Ours: a grand complex!

43
00:02:07,233 --> 00:02:10,133
Their landlord raising the deposit: cruel. Me raising it: just the market rate!

44
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:12,633
Their banners: an eyesore. Ours: team spirit!

45
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:15,867
Double standard: seven, eight, nine!

46
00:02:15,867 --> 00:02:18,600
Dad, did our house go up or down?

47
00:02:18,667 --> 00:02:22,533
…Good question. I checked it every day, and I still don't know.

48
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:26,767
Up or down, my room's the same. And I like this playground.

49
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:30,033
…You're right. It's a home, not a number.

50
00:02:30,167 --> 00:02:33,500
I sold right at the top. It's gonna crash now.

51
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,667
The house you sold just went up again.

52
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:38,267
…Bubble. Total bubble.

53
00:02:38,267 --> 00:02:43,767
The grapes you can't reach are sour. Double standard, number ten.

54
00:02:43,767 --> 00:02:46,167
You said the exact same thing a year ago.

55
00:02:46,167 --> 00:02:49,767
It wasn't the top. That's not a double standard. Just a wrong answer.

56
00:02:49,767 --> 00:02:51,900
…Classic Modapman.
